WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.050 --> 00:01.060
[Disclaimer: This series is created solely for entertainment purposes.

3
00:01.080 --> 00:02.330
All individuals, behaviors, places, and events depicted are entirely fictional,

4
00:02.350 --> 00:05.000
with no intention to represent or reference any organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

5
00:05.020 --> 00:06.800
Whoever dares to take Chris away from me

6
00:06.890 --> 00:07.960
will die.

7
00:07.980 --> 00:09.580
What did she do

8
00:09.600 --> 00:11.930
to make you like her so much that you stayed with her all night?!

9
00:12.100 --> 00:13.610
Let's not be together.

10
00:13.790 --> 00:15.440
It really isn't going to work out.

11
00:15.600 --> 00:17.590
Can you not disappear like that again?

12
00:17.630 --> 00:19.040
If you don't want me to disappear,

13
00:19.600 --> 00:21.600
make me yours, then.

14
00:35.200 --> 00:36.000
Sun...

15
00:37.020 --> 00:37.900
Sun?

16
00:55.700 --> 00:57.390
I'm going out to get some food.

17
00:57.730 --> 00:59.200
I'll come back and make it up to you.

18
01:24.000 --> 01:26.080
[Nadear's father]

19
01:31.150 --> 01:32.000
Yes, Dad?

20
01:33.390 --> 01:34.600
Where have you been?

21
01:34.830 --> 01:37.080
Why did you leave Nadear alone in the hospital?

22
01:37.620 --> 01:39.190
Was she sick?

23
01:39.320 --> 01:41.480
Do you still have the audacity to ask me that?

24
01:43.180 --> 01:44.680
Calm down, dear.

25
02:03.040 --> 02:06.100
[Third Person]

26
02:08.300 --> 02:17.630
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

27
02:18.180 --> 02:23.310
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

28
02:23.340 --> 02:26.950
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

29
02:27.680 --> 02:33.370
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

30
02:33.390 --> 02:42.820
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

31
02:43.220 --> 02:48.270
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

32
02:48.290 --> 02:52.570
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

33
02:52.590 --> 03:01.510
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

34
03:01.980 --> 03:10.110
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

35
03:29.890 --> 03:30.600
Chris,

36
03:31.080 --> 03:32.210
shall we have breakfast?

37
03:49.760 --> 03:50.440
Sun.

38
03:52.500 --> 03:53.280
Chris...

39
03:53.610 --> 03:54.610
What's wrong?

40
03:55.820 --> 03:57.190
Why are you crying?

41
03:58.310 --> 04:00.510
I thought you left me.

42
04:04.520 --> 04:05.460
Poor thing.

43
04:05.480 --> 04:07.080
How could I abandon you?

44
04:08.210 --> 04:10.110
I just went downstairs to look for you.

45
04:12.490 --> 04:14.280
Why did you disappear

46
04:14.300 --> 04:15.760
without leaving me a note?

47
04:16.700 --> 04:18.160
You scared me to death, you know that?

48
04:19.600 --> 04:20.600
Aw...

49
04:21.160 --> 04:22.920
I'm right here now, my love.

50
04:24.780 --> 04:25.710
I have something for you, too.

51
04:29.500 --> 04:30.200
Here.

52
04:31.500 --> 04:32.500
Cute.

53
04:36.290 --> 04:37.520
This is just temporary.

54
04:38.220 --> 04:40.090
When I'm ready to give you the real thing,

55
04:40.110 --> 04:41.280
I'll come back and propose.

56
04:44.310 --> 04:46.080
No taking it back once you've promised.

57
04:52.640 --> 04:54.200
It's only been one night,

58
04:54.220 --> 04:55.320
and you want to get engaged?

59
04:58.500 --> 05:00.090
Aren't you a little too easy?

60
05:02.400 --> 05:03.900
I might be,

61
05:04.520 --> 05:06.280
but only for you, Sun.

62
05:08.980 --> 05:12.000
Because you're the only person who makes me feel the love,

63
05:12.810 --> 05:14.520
and feel loved in return.

64
05:22.010 --> 05:24.090
You're the only person for me too.

65
05:33.620 --> 05:35.300
Shall we go swimming

66
05:35.320 --> 05:36.320
after breakfast?

67
05:40.310 --> 05:41.310
I'm sorry.

68
05:43.240 --> 05:44.760
But I have to leave.

69
05:57.610 --> 05:59.700
To be honest, I don't want to go back yet,

70
06:00.220 --> 06:01.810
but Nadear is sick.

71
06:01.830 --> 06:03.200
There's no one to take care of her.

72
06:04.300 --> 06:07.200
Nadear always took care of me whenever I was sick.

73
06:10.670 --> 06:11.670
You should go.

74
06:12.460 --> 06:13.590
I understand.

75
06:17.520 --> 06:18.300
But...

76
06:18.590 --> 06:20.600
You can trust me.

77
06:21.210 --> 06:23.700
Nadear is just a friend.

78
06:25.400 --> 06:27.600
But you and I are...

79
06:28.520 --> 06:29.640
What are we?

80
06:31.510 --> 06:32.520
"Wives."

81
06:33.470 --> 06:34.510
No way.

82
06:34.770 --> 06:35.670
"Husbands?"

83
06:35.690 --> 06:37.080
Are you crazy?

84
06:38.160 --> 06:39.800
Why don't we become girlfriends first?

85
06:41.680 --> 06:44.000
We'll be that soon enough. Just you wait.

86
06:46.900 --> 06:47.580
Oh!

87
06:48.110 --> 06:49.300
I have something for you.

88
06:51.800 --> 06:52.510
Here.

89
06:53.120 --> 06:55.040
You can stop by if you miss me.

90
06:56.240 --> 06:58.410
You said I'm easy,

91
06:58.730 --> 07:01.300
but giving me your condo keycard isn't being easy at all?

92
07:01.910 --> 07:04.300
Well, everything else is already hard enough.

93
07:16.610 --> 07:19.570
The doctor said she had intestinal inflammation from food poisoning.

94
07:19.590 --> 07:22.830
She's been given antibiotics, so she should feel better soon.

95
07:23.230 --> 07:24.760
And once her IV runs out,

96
07:24.790 --> 07:26.560
she can go home.

97
07:26.800 --> 07:28.910
Dad, Mom, don't worry, okay?

98
07:29.710 --> 07:31.500
Chris can take care of me.

99
07:34.100 --> 07:35.030
Okay.

100
07:35.260 --> 07:37.400
How? She was gone all night.

101
07:38.210 --> 07:39.070
Come on...

102
07:40.880 --> 07:42.440
Please, don't say that to her.

103
07:42.590 --> 07:45.300
She went out to look for ideas for the new dishes.

104
07:46.510 --> 07:47.790
That's why she was busy.

105
07:48.100 --> 07:50.500
It's also my fault for not being careful about what I ate.

106
07:51.920 --> 07:52.820
Hey,

107
07:52.910 --> 07:54.830
how many times have I told you

108
07:54.850 --> 07:57.340
that you've had a weak stomach since you were little?

109
07:57.360 --> 08:00.080
Eating something strange can give you a stomachache.

110
08:00.300 --> 08:01.740
For now,

111
08:01.760 --> 08:04.320
you need to find something light for Nadear to eat, okay?

112
08:05.490 --> 08:06.490
Yes, Mom.

113
08:07.200 --> 08:08.000
Hey, Chris,

114
08:08.600 --> 08:10.190
take care of Nadear, okay?

115
08:12.490 --> 08:13.550
If you leave her

116
08:13.630 --> 08:14.810
this time,

117
08:15.260 --> 08:16.610
I won't forgive you.

118
08:16.640 --> 08:18.200
Come on now, dear.

119
08:18.340 --> 08:20.100
What are you even saying?

120
08:25.800 --> 08:28.190
You don't have to take that to heart.

121
08:30.360 --> 08:31.090
I won't.

122
08:31.910 --> 08:34.590
I understand that your parents are worried about you.

123
08:36.300 --> 08:38.190
Once you get better,

124
08:38.490 --> 08:41.280
I'll tell them that we broke up a long time ago.

125
08:41.890 --> 08:42.890
You can't do that!

126
08:44.620 --> 08:47.830
You promised me you'd stay with me for two more months.

127
08:49.860 --> 08:51.760
I want to take back that promise.

128
08:53.190 --> 08:55.200
But it's just two more months.

129
08:55.500 --> 08:57.850
Can't you hold on a little longer?

130
08:58.480 --> 09:00.710
And I'll give you

131
09:01.190 --> 09:02.630
the rest of your life back.

132
09:04.100 --> 09:06.900
This is the last time

133
09:07.310 --> 09:09.220
I'll ask you for a favor.

134
09:15.070 --> 09:15.790
Alright.

135
09:16.660 --> 09:18.580
If you want two more months,

136
09:18.600 --> 09:20.090
I'll give you that.

137
09:20.470 --> 09:22.800
But only as your friend.

138
09:23.800 --> 09:25.490
Just like I'm doing right now.

139
09:26.010 --> 09:27.130
When a friend gets sick,

140
09:27.990 --> 09:29.230
I'll come to take care of them.

141
09:32.920 --> 09:34.800
This is the first time

142
09:35.900 --> 09:38.130
I don't want to feel better.

143
09:39.900 --> 09:42.020
But I want to see my friend healthy and strong.

144
10:12.340 --> 10:14.090
I brought you your food and medicine.

145
10:14.500 --> 10:16.490
Get some rest after you eat, okay?

146
10:19.000 --> 10:20.810
I'm heading outside for a bit.

147
10:22.620 --> 10:24.010
Will you be back late?

148
10:27.250 --> 10:29.120
I'm not going to complain.

149
10:29.510 --> 10:32.810
Mom and Dad said they'll call me.

150
10:34.280 --> 10:36.580
I'm worried that if they don't see you,

151
10:36.600 --> 10:38.500
they'll come all the way here.

152
10:39.810 --> 10:42.590
Can you come back and talk to my parents?

153
10:44.590 --> 10:45.590
Of course.

154
10:45.620 --> 10:47.210
Since my friend asked, of course I'll do it.

155
10:48.020 --> 10:49.520
Don't forget to eat and take your meds.

156
11:05.830 --> 11:07.620
Surprise!

157
11:19.700 --> 11:21.600
Don't you have someone sick to take care of?

158
11:24.200 --> 11:25.610
Well, I need some time off, too.

159
11:25.850 --> 11:27.550
I'll go back tonight.

160
11:30.130 --> 11:31.490
Here.

161
11:31.670 --> 11:33.340
I got these for you.

162
11:47.960 --> 11:49.200
You remembered...?

163
11:51.540 --> 11:52.790
Remember what?

164
11:54.220 --> 11:56.100
Why did you buy me cheesecake?

165
11:58.180 --> 11:59.300
I didn't mean anything by it.

166
11:59.710 --> 12:01.120
I just thought it looked appetizing.

167
12:05.890 --> 12:06.900
You did.

168
12:07.920 --> 12:09.320
You just don't realize that.

169
12:22.960 --> 12:23.820
How is it?

170
12:26.700 --> 12:27.340
Amazing.

171
12:29.300 --> 12:30.300
Can you feed me too?

172
12:36.470 --> 12:37.470
Oh!

173
12:38.490 --> 12:39.520
Sun!

174
12:39.540 --> 12:40.900
Don't waste it like that.

175
12:48.710 --> 12:49.780
It's not a waste anymore.

176
13:01.110 --> 13:02.110
Chris...

177
13:02.420 --> 13:03.420
Me too.

178
13:18.690 --> 13:20.010
When do you have to go back?

179
13:21.720 --> 13:22.720
Not right now.

180
13:25.210 --> 13:27.210
Can I get my fill of you for now?

181
13:38.300 --> 13:47.920
♫I'm missing all those times you were mine,♫

182
13:47.940 --> 13:52.900
♫But I understand when love runs out of time♫

183
13:52.920 --> 13:57.190
♫I'm no longer the muse inside your heart,♫

184
13:57.210 --> 14:03.080
♫So I'm willing to step away and depart♫

185
14:03.100 --> 14:12.850
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

186
14:12.900 --> 14:17.910
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

187
14:17.930 --> 14:22.150
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

188
14:22.240 --> 14:30.840
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

189
14:31.560 --> 14:39.810
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

190
14:58.610 --> 14:59.520
Chris,

191
15:01.570 --> 15:02.490
wake up.

192
15:03.480 --> 15:04.480
It's late.

193
15:05.020 --> 15:06.320
Don't you have to go home?

194
15:08.450 --> 15:10.220
I'm still sleepy...

195
15:10.800 --> 15:12.390
Just a bit longer...

196
15:52.220 --> 15:54.950
[Third Person]

197
15:56.180 --> 16:00.050
[Third Person]

198
16:27.270 --> 16:28.960
You were so stubborn last night.

199
16:29.560 --> 16:31.060
You refused to get up.

200
16:32.610 --> 16:33.960
Well, I was tired.

201
16:36.060 --> 16:37.470
Don't give me that.

202
16:41.130 --> 16:43.870
I didn't think I'd sleep that long, either.

203
16:44.970 --> 16:47.140
I actually have a really hard time falling asleep.

204
16:47.670 --> 16:49.350
But when I'm with you,

205
16:49.540 --> 16:51.150
I always fall asleep so easily.

206
16:54.200 --> 16:55.860
Are you some kind of sleeping pill?

207
17:00.620 --> 17:02.270
Since when did you have trouble sleeping?

208
17:06.290 --> 17:08.270
Ever since I lost my memories,

209
17:09.230 --> 17:10.570
I've had to rely on sleeping pills.

210
17:17.030 --> 17:18.050
I'm sorry.

211
17:22.370 --> 17:23.870
Why are you apologizing?

212
17:26.800 --> 17:28.670
You talk as if...

213
17:29.620 --> 17:31.380
we know each other again.

214
17:33.450 --> 17:35.260
Is there anything you want to tell me?

215
17:41.600 --> 17:43.500
I'll tell you when the time is right.

216
17:44.550 --> 17:45.970
But for now, you should go back.

217
17:48.960 --> 17:50.790
Don't forget to apologize to her, too.

218
17:54.660 --> 17:56.560
You're not jealous,

219
17:57.170 --> 17:58.650
and you're worried about her too?

220
18:00.250 --> 18:01.570
How nice of you.

221
18:05.060 --> 18:06.670
I'm not a good person.

222
18:08.860 --> 18:10.650
But I'm thankful

223
18:11.350 --> 18:13.070
that she took care of you.

224
18:17.320 --> 18:18.950
What a saint.

225
18:21.330 --> 18:22.460
It's nothing like that.

226
18:27.850 --> 18:29.150
I'm not a good person.

227
18:31.010 --> 18:33.660
If you knew what I've done,

228
18:35.120 --> 18:37.350
you might not love me anymore.

229
19:00.810 --> 19:01.670
Chris?

230
19:07.250 --> 19:08.860
The past is in the past.

231
19:10.340 --> 19:12.260
Right now, I love you.

232
19:13.610 --> 19:14.760
And I won't stop loving you.

233
19:54.270 --> 19:55.410
You're back?

234
19:55.430 --> 19:57.400
Come have breakfast. I ordered this for you.

235
20:03.570 --> 20:04.620
Aren't you angry?

236
20:08.230 --> 20:09.560
I'm more scared.

237
20:11.660 --> 20:14.080
If I got angry and you never come back,

238
20:14.100 --> 20:15.360
what would I do then?

239
20:22.470 --> 20:23.560
I'm sorry.

240
20:25.110 --> 20:27.060
Did your parents call you last night?

241
20:31.180 --> 20:32.250
They did...

242
20:33.470 --> 20:35.650
But I told them you were sleeping.

243
20:36.720 --> 20:38.560
They'll probably call me again today.

244
20:44.160 --> 20:45.680
But don't worry,

245
20:46.620 --> 20:47.870
it might be better to let them

246
20:47.890 --> 20:50.270
slowly get used to not seeing you...

247
21:00.680 --> 21:01.760
Oh, Chris,

248
21:02.160 --> 21:04.720
Nan admitted that she'd embezzled money from our restaurant.

249
21:06.570 --> 21:07.570
Why did she do that?

250
21:09.670 --> 21:12.360
She was struggling financially, so she used the money to pay her mortgage.

251
21:12.650 --> 21:15.070
But she promised she wouldn't do it again.

252
21:15.680 --> 21:18.580
And she'll pay back all the money she took.

253
21:19.270 --> 21:21.760
She only asks to be allowed to keep working at this restaurant.

254
21:23.900 --> 21:25.170
Is that really okay, Nadear?

255
21:27.460 --> 21:29.650
Can you give her another chance?

256
21:31.800 --> 21:35.350
When I left work to take care of you, Nan was the one who

257
21:35.370 --> 21:36.970
took care of our restaurant.

258
21:38.560 --> 21:40.960
That's why she embezzled money from us, too.

259
21:41.660 --> 21:43.760
I'll keep an eye on her.

260
21:45.110 --> 21:47.360
But wasn't Nan able to embezzle money

261
21:47.670 --> 21:49.690
under your watch?

262
21:50.060 --> 21:52.560
If you don't trust me,

263
21:54.230 --> 21:56.750
will you keep an eye on her yourself, then?

264
22:00.280 --> 22:01.280
Of course,

265
22:01.760 --> 22:02.760
I'll do it myself.

266
22:06.960 --> 22:11.020
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

267
22:16.240 --> 22:17.270
Wawah.

268
22:17.570 --> 22:18.660
Are you short on cash lately?

269
22:22.520 --> 22:24.020
Would you like to earn some extra money?

270
22:29.080 --> 22:30.940
Did you bring everything?

271
22:31.770 --> 22:32.950
This one seems broken?

272
22:33.460 --> 22:34.640
Please sign for your delivery.

273
22:37.100 --> 22:38.470
Let me do that for you.

274
22:43.270 --> 22:44.750
Wawah, help me check the items.

275
22:49.880 --> 22:50.860
Wawah,

276
22:50.880 --> 22:52.260
go sort out the stock inside.

277
22:52.450 --> 22:54.140
Let me handle these.

278
22:54.770 --> 22:57.260
I usually do it by myself anyway.

279
22:57.660 --> 22:58.660
It's alright, Nan.

280
22:58.690 --> 23:01.560
Wawah and I will double-check everything this time,

281
23:01.700 --> 23:03.160
so nothing goes missing.

282
23:04.180 --> 23:04.770
Oh, and...

283
23:04.790 --> 23:07.360
from now on, if you're going to order anything or request stock,

284
23:08.200 --> 23:10.020
please let me check it first.

285
23:12.290 --> 23:13.290
Sure thing.

286
23:13.720 --> 23:17.230
I'm glad you're finally...

287
23:17.250 --> 23:19.420
able to do your job like the other shareholders again.

288
23:36.500 --> 23:37.500
Here.

289
24:20.490 --> 24:21.900
I'm hungry.

290
24:25.460 --> 24:27.370
Come over, then.

291
24:27.450 --> 24:29.380
You haven't tasted this in a while.

292
24:36.940 --> 24:38.880
I really want to go,

293
24:38.900 --> 24:40.300
but I have so much work.

294
24:57.140 --> 24:59.460
Come over when you're done working, okay?

295
25:00.970 --> 25:01.810
Oops!

296
25:27.860 --> 25:30.380
[I missed you]

297
25:42.740 --> 25:44.270
Is she really not going to reply?

298
25:44.310 --> 25:45.750
Did work kill her or something?

299
25:50.970 --> 25:51.630
Chris!

300
25:52.080 --> 25:54.680
I missed you too.

301
25:59.280 --> 26:00.650
I came here as soon as I got your message.

302
26:00.670 --> 26:01.750
I even forgot to bring my phone.

303
26:01.770 --> 26:03.260
I thought it was in my pocket.

304
26:04.100 --> 26:06.350
You came all this way just to reply to me?

305
26:09.380 --> 26:10.810
I came to have a taste, too.

306
26:22.780 --> 26:23.620
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

307
26:23.640 --> 26:25.220
If your girlfriend keeps checking up on me like this,

308
26:25.240 --> 26:26.240
I can't stand it.

309
26:28.460 --> 26:31.770
Do you expect Chris to be happy that you embezzled money, then?

310
26:31.960 --> 26:32.940
That's not how it works.

311
26:33.960 --> 26:36.050
If you want to keep working here,

312
26:36.400 --> 26:37.860
you'll have to put up with it.

313
26:38.820 --> 26:40.070
You know full well

314
26:40.090 --> 26:41.730
why things are still this way.

315
26:43.160 --> 26:44.830
Find a way to fix this.

316
26:44.860 --> 26:46.540
Stop her from pestering me.

317
26:46.880 --> 26:48.620
And what am I supposed to do?

318
26:48.970 --> 26:50.770
If you can't think of a way to fix this,

319
26:51.360 --> 26:54.740
should I have her start checking up on you instead?

320
27:19.720 --> 27:21.550
Thank you for coming to see me.

321
27:33.500 --> 27:37.010
How am I supposed to bear watching someone I love be with someone else?

322
27:38.160 --> 27:39.370
What else can you do

323
27:40.740 --> 27:42.270
but bear it?

324
27:43.430 --> 27:45.150
I don't want to bear it.

325
27:46.370 --> 27:48.260
I loved her first.

326
27:49.160 --> 27:51.160
I want her back.

327
27:51.700 --> 27:52.960
We...

328
27:53.670 --> 27:55.890
can't always get what we want, Nadear.

329
27:56.240 --> 27:58.540
Are you a walking quote or something?

330
27:59.580 --> 28:00.650
I know

331
28:00.900 --> 28:03.170
we can't always get what we want,

332
28:03.960 --> 28:06.180
but I only want Chris.

333
28:06.860 --> 28:08.020
She should be mine.

334
28:08.170 --> 28:09.660
Just let Chris go, Nadear.

335
28:10.070 --> 28:11.500
Chris doesn't love you.

336
28:12.100 --> 28:14.450
- Chris loves... - Don't you dare say her name!

337
28:15.360 --> 28:16.750
Chris doesn't love her!

338
28:16.850 --> 28:18.650
She is just misguided.

339
28:19.230 --> 28:21.280
She did all those things to her.

340
28:21.300 --> 28:23.580
How could Chris possibly love her?!

341
28:24.870 --> 28:25.870
Nadear,

342
28:26.180 --> 28:27.180
let go.

343
28:30.110 --> 28:31.960
Chris has to love me.

344
28:34.560 --> 28:36.390
You saw it too.

345
28:37.610 --> 28:39.670
I did everything for her.

346
28:47.650 --> 28:49.790
I won't let her leave me.

347
28:52.870 --> 28:54.770
I'll make her mine.

348
28:57.380 --> 28:59.150
[Verity Skin Clinic]

349
29:02.940 --> 29:03.650
Hey,

350
29:03.870 --> 29:04.960
what should we eat today?

351
29:05.870 --> 29:06.670
Noodles?

352
29:08.230 --> 29:08.940
Yeah.

353
29:09.020 --> 29:11.960
[Verity Skin Clinic]

354
29:12.000 --> 29:13.850
There's a delivery for Ms. Sun.

355
29:16.960 --> 29:18.030
From who?

356
29:18.060 --> 29:19.650
They didn't say anything.

357
29:23.280 --> 29:24.280
Thank you.

358
29:28.750 --> 29:30.860
Aren't there any cards at all?

359
29:32.670 --> 29:34.820
Maybe Chris wanted to surprise me.

360
29:36.560 --> 29:38.540
It could be someone else, too.

361
29:38.570 --> 29:40.540
Those puppies and wolves

362
29:40.560 --> 29:43.280
who like to flirt with you in your DMs.

363
29:44.410 --> 29:45.650
Those people don't know

364
29:45.670 --> 29:46.860
what I like.

365
29:48.870 --> 29:50.760
Only Chris knows that.

366
29:52.000 --> 29:52.800
Yeah.

367
30:00.060 --> 30:02.350
The files documenting all the money Nan embezzled from the restaurant

368
30:02.370 --> 30:03.450
are here.

369
30:05.170 --> 30:06.960
She really made two versions of the bills,

370
30:06.990 --> 30:09.260
just as you suspected.

371
30:09.280 --> 30:10.450
That's not nice.

372
30:12.660 --> 30:14.580
Thank you so much for helping me, Wawah.

373
30:14.600 --> 30:16.160
I'll handle the rest.

374
30:16.180 --> 30:17.250
You should get back to work.

375
30:18.060 --> 30:20.270
Just let me know if you need any help.

376
30:20.290 --> 30:22.260
I love this restaurant too.

377
30:23.450 --> 30:25.410
I don't know how Nan could do that.

378
30:25.750 --> 30:27.670
Doesn't she feel bad for Nadear?

379
30:27.690 --> 30:29.650
She is so frugal.

380
30:29.860 --> 30:32.780
I even saw Nadear taking spoiled milk home once.

381
30:34.660 --> 30:36.650
Probably for watering her plants.

382
30:37.680 --> 30:38.680
Wait,

383
30:39.640 --> 30:41.340
when did Nadear take spoiled milk home?

384
30:45.970 --> 30:47.790
I think...

385
30:48.330 --> 30:50.170
it was the day before she took sick leave.

386
30:50.680 --> 30:51.780
Why?

387
30:54.460 --> 30:55.460
It's nothing.

388
30:55.680 --> 30:56.780
You can get back to work.

389
30:57.570 --> 30:58.270
Yes.

390
31:12.960 --> 31:15.260
Thanks for sending me this.

391
31:17.770 --> 31:18.540
Should I eat it?

392
31:19.860 --> 31:21.860
Go ahead and clog your arteries.

393
31:33.120 --> 31:34.300
Don't eat that cake, Sun.

394
31:35.060 --> 31:36.060
Why?

395
31:36.220 --> 31:37.140
I'll tell you later.

396
31:37.260 --> 31:38.660
Keep that cake.

397
31:38.860 --> 31:40.540
And don't eat it, no matter what.

398
31:46.750 --> 31:49.460
[Third Person]

399
31:50.693 --> 31:54.563
[Third Person]

400
32:00.623 --> 32:01.353
Chris,

401
32:01.893 --> 32:02.893
we have to talk.

402
32:03.163 --> 32:04.473
Not now, Nan.

403
32:04.693 --> 32:05.643
We have to talk now.

404
32:06.733 --> 32:07.973
You changed the restaurant's password.

405
32:07.993 --> 32:09.563
Why didn't you let me access the restaurant's accounts?

406
32:13.243 --> 32:14.843
Then why did you steal money from the restaurant?

407
32:18.983 --> 32:20.463
I already told you I'd pay it back.

408
32:20.483 --> 32:21.963
Is it that hard to understand?

409
32:22.223 --> 32:23.053
Give me the password.

410
32:24.163 --> 32:25.553
You're the one who doesn't understand.

411
32:25.863 --> 32:26.903
Didn't you say you wouldn't do it again?

412
32:26.923 --> 32:28.133
Yet you're still doing it.

413
32:28.563 --> 32:30.263
Do you think I'm that stupid?

414
32:31.383 --> 32:33.253
I just borrowed a little money.

415
32:33.543 --> 32:34.363
What's the big deal?

416
32:35.503 --> 32:37.493
You never used to speak up like this before.

417
32:38.863 --> 32:40.563
I'm your goddamn senior.

418
32:43.373 --> 32:45.163
What kind of goddamn senior steals money from their junior?

419
32:46.183 --> 32:48.033
You can talk to my lawyer after this.

420
32:49.463 --> 32:51.243
Are you threatening me with a lawyer?

421
32:51.663 --> 32:52.663
I'm not.

422
32:53.053 --> 32:54.663
But if you keep acting like this,

423
32:54.683 --> 32:55.923
then you're going to jail.

424
32:57.433 --> 32:58.323
- F*ck you! - Ow!

425
32:59.683 --> 33:01.043
- Nan... Nan! - Nan!

426
33:01.063 --> 33:02.223
Have you lost your mind?!

427
33:02.293 --> 33:04.143
- Nan, don't! - Let go of me!

428
33:07.053 --> 33:07.843
Nadear...

429
33:18.383 --> 33:19.573
Is it really just a sprain?

430
33:19.593 --> 33:22.363
You're not lying to me about having a fracture, are you?

431
33:22.583 --> 33:25.353
No, it's just a sprained ankle.

432
33:25.583 --> 33:27.253
Don't worry.

433
33:36.973 --> 33:37.973
Yes, Wawah?

434
33:38.003 --> 33:40.073
Are you with Nadear?

435
33:43.573 --> 33:44.863
No, what is it?

436
33:44.893 --> 33:47.223
Before you got into a fight with Nan,

437
33:47.243 --> 33:48.863
I happened to hear...

438
33:48.883 --> 33:50.733
You really want me to do this?

439
33:50.753 --> 33:51.553
Yeah.

440
33:51.983 --> 33:53.573
Push me as hard as you can.

441
33:53.763 --> 33:55.233
Are you crazy?

442
33:55.253 --> 33:56.043
Why would I push you?

443
33:56.273 --> 33:58.433
If you want this to end, you have to do it.

444
34:01.373 --> 34:04.353
I even saw Nadear taking spoiled milk home once.

445
34:04.463 --> 34:06.553
Probably for watering her plants.

446
34:07.753 --> 34:09.273
This is the first time

447
34:10.773 --> 34:13.163
I don't want to feel better.

448
34:21.063 --> 34:21.863
Chris.

449
34:33.273 --> 34:36.753
My parents are asking if you can take care of me for a while.

450
34:36.783 --> 34:38.893
If you can't, they'll take care of me themselves.

451
34:41.123 --> 34:42.153
Of course,

452
34:43.043 --> 34:44.683
I'll take care of you.

453
34:47.803 --> 34:49.263
See?

454
34:49.653 --> 34:52.663
Chris can take care of me. You don't have to worry.

455
34:56.763 --> 34:58.953
[Pork congee]

456
34:59.753 --> 35:01.363
Nadear hurt herself?!

457
35:04.473 --> 35:05.863
Yeah...

458
35:06.113 --> 35:09.323
I think she did it to keep me close,

459
35:10.073 --> 35:13.523
so I was afraid she might hurt you too.

460
35:14.663 --> 35:17.773
I really didn't send you that cheesecake.

461
35:19.863 --> 35:22.683
I sent the cake to my friend to have it tested for contaminants.

462
35:22.953 --> 35:24.573
The results should be out soon.

463
35:28.173 --> 35:29.173
Okay.

464
35:36.963 --> 35:37.963
Chris...

465
35:39.793 --> 35:42.253
Aside from Nadear hurting herself,

466
35:43.243 --> 35:44.853
are you sure

467
35:45.373 --> 35:47.373
that what you're doing isn't hurting her too?

468
35:51.783 --> 35:53.283
I understand

469
35:53.783 --> 35:56.563
that you're taking care of her as a friend.

470
35:58.373 --> 35:59.973
I'm not saying this because I'm jealous,

471
36:01.373 --> 36:03.473
but I'm worried about you.

472
36:09.553 --> 36:11.263
Are you saying that...

473
36:11.773 --> 36:13.053
what I'm doing

474
36:13.073 --> 36:15.393
is still giving Nadear false hope?

475
36:17.373 --> 36:19.573
Don't you think so?

476
36:21.703 --> 36:23.153
Ow!

477
36:24.613 --> 36:25.383
Nadear.

478
36:26.663 --> 36:28.163
Nadear, are you okay?

479
36:28.663 --> 36:29.963
Can I come in?

480
36:30.763 --> 36:32.083
Go ahead.

481
36:34.693 --> 36:35.843
Is everything alright?

482
36:36.063 --> 36:37.953
It's so hard to shower.

483
36:38.853 --> 36:40.443
Can you help me?

484
36:44.983 --> 36:47.173
Here, this should make it easier now.

485
36:47.193 --> 36:49.333
I told you I'd take care of you.

486
36:51.873 --> 36:53.723
You're such a good friend, huh?

487
36:54.183 --> 36:54.973
Yeah,

488
36:55.003 --> 36:56.863
I'll be a good friend to you.

489
36:57.263 --> 36:59.533
Hurry and shower before you catch a cold, okay?

490
36:59.553 --> 37:00.663
I'm leaving now.

491
37:03.373 --> 37:04.273
Chris.

492
37:04.293 --> 37:06.153
Chris, where are you going?!

493
37:22.863 --> 37:24.883
When a friend pours you water,

494
37:25.463 --> 37:26.553
you don't think much of it.

495
37:28.073 --> 37:29.943
But if it's someone you like,

496
37:30.283 --> 37:31.573
even pouring you water

497
37:32.773 --> 37:34.583
can feel special.

498
37:41.863 --> 37:43.863
When a friend shares something they like with you,

499
37:44.683 --> 37:46.063
you just see it as a kind gesture.

500
37:47.263 --> 37:49.373
But when someone you like does it,

501
37:50.473 --> 37:51.973
you assume they like you back.

502
37:55.973 --> 37:56.973
Mm.

503
37:57.453 --> 37:58.933
The same action...

504
37:58.953 --> 38:00.033
but seen differently.

505
38:06.373 --> 38:07.263
Oh no.

506
38:07.943 --> 38:09.463
What will she think

507
38:10.263 --> 38:11.893
if I bathe her?

508
38:12.263 --> 38:13.053
Chris?!

509
38:15.813 --> 38:17.323
It's nothing...

510
38:17.343 --> 38:18.683
Nadear just asked me for help,

511
38:18.703 --> 38:19.963
so I helped her.

512
38:20.983 --> 38:22.063
Should you be doing that?

513
38:28.043 --> 38:30.403
This is far worse than giving false hope.

514
38:30.733 --> 38:31.983
Whoa, whoa, uh...

515
38:34.423 --> 38:35.273
Is this

516
38:35.613 --> 38:37.533
what you call being jealous?

517
38:42.403 --> 38:43.663
You still have to ask that?

518
38:44.643 --> 38:46.553
If Nadear hurts herself again,

519
38:46.883 --> 38:48.453
just know that it's because of you.

520
38:50.773 --> 38:52.853
Just kidding.

521
38:53.003 --> 38:55.583
I just don't want to see you looking sad anymore.

522
38:56.023 --> 38:58.443
I want to see your grumpy face, too.

523
39:03.903 --> 39:06.833
If I know what upsets you,

524
39:07.753 --> 39:09.363
I won't do it.

525
39:13.563 --> 39:14.783
Because...

526
39:15.183 --> 39:17.663
I've already upset you enough.

527
39:26.273 --> 39:26.863
Here.

528
39:27.603 --> 39:29.523
Eat up, baby.

529
39:30.213 --> 39:32.283
I give you this because

530
39:32.303 --> 39:34.443
I care about you and love you.

531
39:36.163 --> 39:37.493
What's with the "baby"?

532
39:37.773 --> 39:38.773
You idiot.

533
39:39.773 --> 39:40.733
Aha,

534
39:40.753 --> 39:42.503
you liked that, didn't you?

535
39:42.523 --> 39:43.643
Look at you smiling.

536
39:49.623 --> 39:51.643
Don't be sad.

537
39:52.553 --> 39:53.553
Eat this too.

538
39:55.853 --> 39:57.553
Here's the dish.

539
40:09.893 --> 40:11.193
Aren't we getting out together?

540
40:14.253 --> 40:17.713
I forgot we can't go public yet.

541
40:18.643 --> 40:21.483
I'd rather you spend time with your friend.

542
40:21.513 --> 40:23.953
And there are doctors looking to invest in your business, too.

543
40:25.073 --> 40:28.083
But if you want to go public, I can get out with you now.

544
40:28.763 --> 40:29.773
It's okay.

545
40:30.713 --> 40:33.273
You cared about my friend,

546
40:33.773 --> 40:36.463
so I'll care about your friend, too.

547
40:37.363 --> 40:37.893
But...

548
40:39.053 --> 40:40.293
just friends, okay?

549
40:42.773 --> 40:43.273
Yeah.

550
40:44.263 --> 40:45.193
Then...

551
40:45.583 --> 40:47.063
I won't look forward to helping my friend take a bath anymore.

552
40:48.183 --> 40:50.273
I'll only look forward to helping my girlfriend take a bath.

553
40:55.663 --> 40:56.353
Wait.

554
40:59.813 --> 41:00.463
Here.

555
41:01.343 --> 41:02.563
In case you feel cold, Doc.

556
41:05.683 --> 41:06.763
Thank you.

557
41:07.613 --> 41:09.163
If you want to go home, call me, okay?

558
41:09.273 --> 41:10.063
I'll come pick you up.

559
41:10.083 --> 41:10.603
Mm.

560
41:11.273 --> 41:12.273
Okay.

561
41:13.493 --> 41:14.673
- Bye-bye. - Bye-bye.

562
41:33.853 --> 41:35.433
Where is Air?

563
41:36.283 --> 41:37.673
She's on her way.

564
41:41.453 --> 41:42.093
Oh,

565
41:42.863 --> 41:44.463
there are clinics everywhere,

566
41:44.483 --> 41:46.463
so why do they want to invest in us?

567
41:46.913 --> 41:48.083
I don't know either.

568
41:48.593 --> 41:50.953
But... I want Air as a shareholder,

569
41:51.253 --> 41:52.663
'cause she's pretty.

570
41:52.873 --> 41:53.873
Ugh.

571
41:54.783 --> 41:55.783
No wonder

572
41:55.803 --> 41:57.433
you asked her to meet up here.

573
41:57.453 --> 41:58.753
You plan to get her drunk, huh?

574
41:58.933 --> 42:00.243
Are you crazy?

575
42:04.253 --> 42:05.283
She called me.

576
42:08.973 --> 42:10.253
Hello, Air?

577
42:10.823 --> 42:12.373
Oh, you're here?

578
42:12.673 --> 42:14.563
I'm at the bar with my friend.

579
42:19.973 --> 42:21.473
Is that pretty woman

580
42:21.863 --> 42:23.273
Air?

581
42:24.663 --> 42:25.663
Yeah.

582
42:31.573 --> 42:33.083
So why...

583
42:33.163 --> 42:34.873
is Aek with her?

584
42:40.523 --> 42:41.663
I didn't know...

585
42:41.683 --> 42:44.033
Air knew your ex.

586
42:50.073 --> 42:51.383
- Hello, Air. - Hello.

587
42:51.403 --> 42:52.313
Hello.

588
42:52.333 --> 42:53.593
Hello.

589
43:09.393 --> 43:12.153
Sa-run is also interested in your skin clinic,

590
43:12.533 --> 43:14.273
so I brought him here.

591
43:15.123 --> 43:16.543
I just found out...

592
43:17.003 --> 43:18.773
you two already know each other.

593
43:18.963 --> 43:20.153
It's a small world, huh?

594
43:25.163 --> 43:26.463
Um, one second.

595
43:28.693 --> 43:30.123
Hello?

596
43:30.473 --> 43:32.253
Yes, I'll be there soon.

597
43:34.863 --> 43:35.643
Uh...

598
43:36.173 --> 43:37.173
I...

599
43:37.353 --> 43:39.173
have an urgent case.

600
43:39.403 --> 43:42.633
Can we meet up again some other time?

601
43:42.853 --> 43:44.443
Oh, let me walk you out.

602
43:44.693 --> 43:45.483
Okay.

603
43:45.893 --> 43:46.943
See you later.

604
43:46.983 --> 43:48.123
I'll be right back.

605
43:49.043 --> 43:49.963
It won't take long.

606
43:54.463 --> 43:55.793
Since when did you come back?

607
43:56.373 --> 43:57.863
Why haven't I heard about this?

608
43:59.153 --> 44:00.473
I missed you, Sun.

609
44:01.863 --> 44:03.453
What is there to miss?

610
44:03.963 --> 44:05.353
We only dated for two months.

611
44:05.753 --> 44:06.853
We met a few times

612
44:07.383 --> 44:08.443
before we broke up.

613
44:10.043 --> 44:11.733
Well, other than my family,

614
44:12.443 --> 44:13.443
you're the only one

615
44:13.773 --> 44:14.873
who calls me Aek.

616
44:15.883 --> 44:17.033
Perhaps I missed you

617
44:17.053 --> 44:18.053
because of that.

618
44:19.183 --> 44:20.453
Don't you think

619
44:20.893 --> 44:22.753
we ended things a bit too abruptly?

620
44:23.913 --> 44:24.763
You know

621
44:24.783 --> 44:26.353
why we dated back then.

622
44:26.383 --> 44:28.663
I let you use me to make other people jealous,

623
44:29.873 --> 44:31.263
but I actually love you now.

624
44:33.133 --> 44:34.133
To be honest,

625
44:35.793 --> 44:36.963
I've always had feelings for you.

626
44:46.583 --> 44:50.853
[I'll be back soon. Air is still waiting for her ride]

627
44:54.123 --> 44:55.363
We should meet up another time

628
44:55.873 --> 44:57.173
since we're not all here anyway.

629
44:59.033 --> 45:00.773
But I want to talk to you about something.

630
45:02.363 --> 45:03.673
Did you like the cheesecake?

631
45:05.983 --> 45:07.063
Cheesecake?

632
45:08.713 --> 45:09.883
Did you send that to me?

633
45:09.903 --> 45:11.043
It's delicious, wasn't it?

634
45:11.673 --> 45:13.553
How did you know I like cheesecake?

635
45:14.303 --> 45:16.453
Why didn't you tell me you sent it?

636
45:16.473 --> 45:18.153
How did you know where I work?

637
45:19.663 --> 45:20.663
Calm down.

638
45:22.063 --> 45:24.053
I knew I'd see you soon,

639
45:24.483 --> 45:25.873
so I wanted to surprise you.

640
45:27.803 --> 45:30.243
Who told you I like cheesecake?

641
45:31.493 --> 45:33.143
If you want to know,

642
45:35.063 --> 45:36.573
then have a few more drinks with me.

643
45:52.643 --> 45:55.473
Things aren't great right now.

644
45:55.493 --> 45:57.163
Can you come pick me up?

645
46:02.073 --> 46:05.263
[Third Person]

646
46:06.544 --> 46:10.334
[Third Person]

647
46:14.744 --> 46:15.894
When are you going to tell me

648
46:16.034 --> 46:17.534
who told you?

649
46:17.854 --> 46:19.124
No one told me.

650
46:20.554 --> 46:21.554
I just...

651
46:21.854 --> 46:22.854
guessed.

652
46:25.904 --> 46:27.454
How could you guess my address right?

653
46:27.884 --> 46:29.244
Don't lie to me.

654
46:29.684 --> 46:31.554
I know this isn't a coincidence.

655
46:31.854 --> 46:33.034
Tonight, too.

656
46:42.854 --> 46:43.514
Yes.

657
46:45.374 --> 46:47.024
I knew you were back,

658
46:48.214 --> 46:49.824
so I came to see you.

659
46:55.524 --> 46:57.634
I really want us to get back together.

660
46:59.424 --> 47:01.554
If you really want us to get back together,

661
47:01.764 --> 47:02.834
you'll have to tell me

662
47:02.854 --> 47:04.034
who told you.

663
47:19.014 --> 47:20.214
My junior,

664
47:21.944 --> 47:22.944
Nadear.

665
47:25.644 --> 47:27.234
You know her, don't you?

666
47:28.274 --> 47:30.624
She asked me about you

667
47:30.704 --> 47:32.154
four years ago

668
47:32.174 --> 47:33.664
when you had an accident.

669
47:38.304 --> 47:39.304
Where are you going?

670
47:39.324 --> 47:40.024
Sun.

671
47:41.954 --> 47:42.954
Would you like the check now?

672
47:48.124 --> 47:49.124
I'm sorry!

673
47:51.074 --> 47:52.344
Let's exchange IGs,

674
47:52.774 --> 47:53.934
and I'll forgive you.

675
47:55.044 --> 47:56.924
I'm not interested, sorry.

676
47:57.224 --> 47:58.354
Wait.

677
47:58.374 --> 47:59.694
Playing hard to get, huh?

678
48:00.144 --> 48:01.524
It's just your IG.

679
48:01.744 --> 48:03.124
Why are you being so cold?

680
48:03.934 --> 48:05.294
I'm sorry, but no.

681
48:05.314 --> 48:06.624
What's the rush?

682
48:06.644 --> 48:07.814
Let go, please.

683
48:12.764 --> 48:14.644
She said no. Don't you get it?

684
48:15.004 --> 48:16.134
Or do I have to call the police?

685
48:18.424 --> 48:18.954
Chris...

686
48:20.494 --> 48:22.444
Oh...

687
48:22.674 --> 48:24.744
A jealous friend.

688
48:25.754 --> 48:26.854
Not her friend.

689
48:30.104 --> 48:30.614
Girlfriend.

690
48:34.734 --> 48:35.544
That's right.

691
48:35.994 --> 48:36.644
Girlfriend.

692
48:37.454 --> 48:38.454
Goodbye now.

693
48:45.344 --> 48:46.434
You got here so fast.

694
48:47.334 --> 48:48.834
I'm here to pick up a drunk girl.

695
48:49.134 --> 48:50.134
How drunk are you?

696
48:50.344 --> 48:51.454
Just a little.

697
48:52.234 --> 48:53.304
Come on, let's go home.

698
48:53.324 --> 48:54.134
Mm.

699
48:55.754 --> 48:56.754
Oh, Chris.

700
49:01.604 --> 49:02.854
Isn't Nadear with you?

701
49:08.234 --> 49:09.234
No, she isn't.

702
49:10.104 --> 49:12.734
I met Nadear's parents a few days ago.

703
49:13.534 --> 49:14.534
They said you

704
49:14.564 --> 49:15.904
and Nadear are going to get married.

705
49:18.694 --> 49:19.934
Don't forget to invite me, too.

706
49:22.844 --> 49:23.534
Yes.

707
49:29.554 --> 49:30.554
Sun, I'll drive you home.

708
49:30.574 --> 49:31.424
No need.

709
49:31.554 --> 49:32.554
I'll drive her home.

710
49:48.474 --> 49:49.834
How can we get back together

711
49:51.044 --> 49:52.744
if you don't take care of your girl?

712
49:53.854 --> 49:55.654
Chris came to take Sun home.

713
50:10.254 --> 50:12.404
[I bought this for you, Nadear]

714
50:23.284 --> 50:24.284
Are you cold?

715
50:28.444 --> 50:30.644
I'm sorry for upsetting you.

716
50:30.944 --> 50:33.814
Sa-run is close to Nadear's parents.

717
50:34.424 --> 50:35.894
I'm sorry

718
50:36.364 --> 50:37.974
for getting upset

719
50:38.374 --> 50:41.664
when I'm supposed to be someone you can feel at ease with.

720
50:42.144 --> 50:43.514
You always have been,

721
50:44.754 --> 50:45.754
until earlier.

722
50:49.794 --> 50:52.134
I shouldn't have left you alone.

723
50:52.804 --> 50:54.754
Just thinking that something bad might happen to you

724
50:54.774 --> 50:56.324
makes my heart sink.

725
50:57.464 --> 50:58.464
That's right.

726
50:59.304 --> 51:01.334
I fell in love with you

727
51:02.634 --> 51:05.334
who always protect others.

728
51:07.094 --> 51:07.824
Hm?

729
51:10.644 --> 51:12.534
Well...what I mean is,

730
51:12.834 --> 51:13.924
I'm alright now.

731
51:14.224 --> 51:16.134
I have you here with me.

732
51:20.044 --> 51:22.204
Oh, when you said

733
51:22.224 --> 51:23.824
things weren't great,

734
51:24.484 --> 51:26.674
was it because of Sa-run?

735
51:27.054 --> 51:28.054
Mm...

736
51:28.904 --> 51:31.304
Aek was the one who sent me that cheesecake,

737
51:32.474 --> 51:34.024
but at least it wasn't Nadear's doing.

738
51:34.644 --> 51:36.634
She didn't mean to hurt anyone,

739
51:37.874 --> 51:39.214
only herself.

740
51:39.634 --> 51:40.924
That's a relief.

741
51:42.804 --> 51:43.544
It's not.

742
51:44.754 --> 51:45.754
Why?

743
51:47.524 --> 51:48.454
I'm jealous.

744
51:58.434 --> 51:59.434
You can be jealous,

745
52:00.124 --> 52:01.334
but don't stress too much.

746
52:03.154 --> 52:05.634
Because you're the only one

747
52:07.044 --> 52:08.834
I have feelings for, Chris.

748
52:15.194 --> 52:16.934
Okay.

749
52:17.274 --> 52:19.374
We should go home.

750
52:20.134 --> 52:21.364
Because

751
52:21.384 --> 52:22.284
your girlfriend here

752
52:22.304 --> 52:24.674
is going to give you a bath as a reward.

753
52:25.194 --> 52:26.414
Chris!

754
52:26.494 --> 52:27.414
Are you crazy?

755
52:27.784 --> 52:28.854
You don't want to?

756
52:29.654 --> 52:30.154
Hm?

757
52:31.714 --> 52:33.054
Come on, let's go home.

758
52:33.084 --> 52:34.724
Let's go.

759
52:35.034 --> 52:35.824
Let's go home.

760
53:05.934 --> 53:07.534
How did you know my size?

761
53:10.324 --> 53:11.624
How could I not?

762
53:23.834 --> 53:25.594
Hm, come here.

763
53:26.984 --> 53:27.934
Are you cold?

764
53:28.474 --> 53:29.254
I'm okay.

765
53:29.954 --> 53:32.324
Why...did you bring me here?

766
53:32.344 --> 53:33.804
Weren't we going home?

767
53:37.624 --> 53:40.484
Well, you said you wanted to swim when we went to the beach,

768
53:40.824 --> 53:42.224
but I had to go back first.

769
53:43.254 --> 53:45.534
So I brought you here to swim today.

770
53:47.344 --> 53:48.354
Thank you

771
53:49.114 --> 53:51.214
